# A list that grows, written in Ovis (generics.md §8): room for its items,
# made bigger when it is full, as the built-in list's storage is.
a growing list of (item) has:
    data (pointer to many items)
    count (whole number, 0)
    room (whole number, 0)

to add (x: any item) to the end of (xs: growing list of item):
    if count of xs = room of xs:
        bigger = room of xs * 2 + 4
        data of xs = data of xs grown to bigger items from room of xs
        room of xs = bigger
    set the item at (data of xs moved by count of xs items) to x
    increase count of xs by 1

# Items count from 1, as the built-in list's do, and are checked.
to item (i: whole number) of (xs: growing list of any item):
    if i < 1 or i > count of xs:
        show "There is no item", i, "of a growing list of", count of xs
        end the program
    give back the item at (data of xs moved by (i - 1) items)

to release (xs: growing list of any item):
    free data of xs
    free xs
